WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.400
Whether you're a Scrooge stan or you've already
broken out your favorite holiday sweater,

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.040
Netflix is hoping to make those long, cold
winter nights more bearable with its December

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:09.720
offerings.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.540
Here's all the best stuff coming to Netflix
in December 2019.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.040
Did you feel that?

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.720
It was a shiver going down your spine… and
you'd better get used to it.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.300
Netflix will be streaming quite a few thrillers
and chillers in December 2019.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.860
The question is: Can you handle it?

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.580
On December 1st, you can hunker down and watch
Dead Kids.

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:34.820
This Filipino film involves a gang of teenagers
who attempt to kidnap an arrogant school bully.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.060
Things get complicated… and very dark indeed.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.880
Then, on December 9th, you should brace yourself
for the 2017 critical darling It Comes At

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.400
Night.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.500
The film centers around two families, both
of whom are toughing it out in a post-apocalyptic

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.510
world.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.720
Expect plenty of paranoia, doom, dread, and
death.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:54.700
Happy holidays!

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.820
On December 25th, Sweetheart starts streaming
on Netflix.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.300
The film tells the story of Jenn, a frantic
shipwreck survivor played by Kiersey Clemons.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.760
Thanks to a nocturnal sea monster, the very
real possibility of starving to death is the

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.520
very least of her concerns.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.200
And if you're in the mood for handsome, bookish
stalkers that like to kill people, we've got

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.060
just the ticket.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.860
The Netflix creep-fest You is back for a second
season on December 25th.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.900
You're going to love it.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.180
Like, really, really love it.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.480
“You'll realize I'm not a maybe.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.060
I'm the one."

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.280
Netflix has loaded its December schedule with
tons of stand-up specials.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.700
On December 3rd, Tiffany Haddish gives us
Black Mitzvah, which finds the actress and

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.480
comedian discussing her Jewish roots and her
growing success — but funny!

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.180
Then, on December 12th, British comedian Jack
Whitehall gives us Christmas with my Father

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.640
… which will find Whitehall and his dad
sharing a West End stage for a night of laughs.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:57.200
That brings us to John Mulaney &amp; The Sack
Lunch Bunch, which debuts on December 24th.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.299
Pitched as an old-school variety show and
designed in the style of Mister Rogers' Neighborhood,

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:06.200
the special features celebrity guests like
Natasha Lyonne and Jake Gyllenhaal trying

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.280
to entertain children.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.720
Anything with Mulaney deserves your undivided
attention, so you'll definitely want to get

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.340
in on the action.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.520
On December 10th, we'll be getting Michelle
Wolf: Joke Show, a new special from the comedian

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.880
who roasted the Trump administration at the
2018 White House Correspondents' Dinner.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:27.240
Expect her to touch upon any number of hot-button
issues… including "woke" culture, modern-day

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.920
feminism, and much, much more.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.360
If that sounds too high-minded, not to worry:
All three Austin Powers films will be hitting

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.200
the streaming service on December 1st.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.840
Consider it a Christmastime miracle.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.860
"Well if I'm preaching to the converted, why
are you being so slavish to the three question

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.120
form is my question?

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.780
You're not even looking at me man.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.760
Now you're just being rude."

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:50.660
Perhaps you'd rather explore the grittier
side of life.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.100
Let it suffice to say, plenty of dramatic
fare is on the way.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.360
On December 6th, you can finally see whether
or not Marriage Story is worth all the hype.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.560
Directed by Noah Baumbach, the film stars
Scarlett Johansson and Adam Driver as a couple

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.070
whose marriage is disintegrating.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.360
Needless to say, it's some heavy stuff.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.980
"How are you doing?"

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.820
On December 1st, you can get embroiled in
Spike Lee's incredible biopic Malcolm X, starring

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.220
Denzel Washington.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.080
Or perhaps you'd rather explore The Danish
Girl, a moving romantic drama starring Eddie

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:25.580
Redmayne?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.660
That one begins streaming on December 16th.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.520
Then, on December 29th, you can take a look
at the action-drama Lawless.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:38.400
The film stars Shia LaBeouf and Tom Hardy
as two fast-driving bootleggers in Prohibition-era

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.020
Virginia.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.720
Expect lots of shootouts.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.760
Let's say it's a cold night in December and
you're craving some adventure.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.540
Not to worry: Netflix has got you covered.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.900
On December 13th, you can sink your teeth
into 6 Underground, directed by Michael Bay.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.500
It stars Ryan Reynolds as the leader of a
group of six professional criminals, all of

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.300
whom have faked their own deaths.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.840
"Best part of being dead… is the freedom."

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.290
On December 8th, the spy thriller From Paris
with Love will instantly add some intrigue

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:08.960
to your life.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.380
The film stars Jonathan Rhys Meyers and an
almost-unrecognizable John Travolta as two

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.220
agents trying to thwart terrorist plots in
Paris.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:18.800
And that's not all.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.740
On December 31st, you can start streaming
four James Bond movies starring Pierce Brosnan

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.760
— including Die Another Day, GoldenEye,
Tomorrow Never Dies, and The World Is Not

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:29.260
Enough.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.659
Netflix is banking on a lot of monstrous fantasy
fare at the end of the year.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.340
On December 5th, V Wars will be coming your
way.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:42.420
Based on the popular comic books, the series
stars Ian Somerhalder as a doctor trying to

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.700
save people from a virus that turns them into…
you guessed it... vampires.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.100
And he's not the only square-jawed heartthrob
on the lookout for creepos.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:57.300
The Witcher debuts on December 20th, starring
Superman's Henry Cavill as a blonde, mysterious

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.800
monster hunter named Geralt of Rivia.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.180
The series is an adaptation of the popular
fantasy novels and short stories by Polish

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.000
author Andrzej Sapkowski.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.180
"They say witches can't feel human emotion.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.860
What do you believe in?"

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.620
Craving some science fiction?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.480
You're in luck.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.680
Lost in Space returns to the streamer on December
24th.

00:05:17.909 --> 00:05:23.090
And now for the festive stuff: A Christmas
Prince 3: The Royal Baby is set for release

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.080
on December 5th.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.000
As you may recall, 2017's A Christmas Prince
involved an American journalist named Amber

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:34.129
— played by Rose McIver — who falls for
a royal named Richard, played by Ben Lamb.

00:05:34.129 --> 00:05:38.270
After last year's A Christmas Prince: The
Royal Wedding, Queen Amber is pregnant with

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:42.520
the couple's first child — and she's also
out to solve a mystery that involves a missing

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.420
peace treaty.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.310
"Who in this palace had the means, the opportunity,
the motive…?"

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.310
"If the sacred truce is broken….

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.919
There will be a curse on the firstborn child."

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:55.669
And here's another festive sequel for you:
A Cinderella Story: Christmas Wish is the

00:05:55.669 --> 00:06:00.340
fifth installment of the film franchise that
began with 2004's A Cinderella Story.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.200
That one starred Hilary Duff and Chad Michael
Murray.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.640
In the latest installment, an aspiring singer
named Kat — played by Laura Marano must

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.220
overcome her "wicked" stepfamily in order
to perform at a gala.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.200
Meanwhile, she's falling head over heels for
a certain special someone.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.220
Will love prevail in the end?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.939
All these questions and more will be answered...
when A Cinderella Story: Christmas Wish hits

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.680
Netflix on December 1st.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.380
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.680
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:06:31.689 --> 00:06:34.819
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

